039829/assets/48de26c11ae08afb45ec19ee56e770f7418f9be2afb8ee7dd46a0d1136cb125b.png)" 13194139534701 true] [17592186092060 1100 "Find the expression that gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=t, \\, y=\\ln{(\\cos{t})}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ (see graph below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/48de26c11ae08afb45ec19ee56e770f7418f9be2afb8ee7dd46a0d1136cb125b.png)" 13194139534701 false] [17592186092322 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304318 13194139534701 true] [17592186092322 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304325 13194139534701 true] [17592186092322 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304332 13194139534701 true] [17592186092323 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304339 13194139534701 true] [17592186092324 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304304 13194139534701 true] [17592186092324 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304311 13194139534701 true] [17592186092324 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304346 13194139534701 true] [17592186092324 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304350 13194139534701 true] [17592186092324 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304353 13194139534701 true] [17592186092521 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534701 true] [17592186092521 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/assets/80577a585741748702b61596db84983592ecbc6c01fca78af033bf82dbe62ad2.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={e}^{t},\\,y={e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\nfrom $t=-3$ to $t=1$ (shown above)?" 13194139534701 true] [17592186092521 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/997/Source/Images/q-15185.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x = e^{t}, y = e^{t}\\sin t$\nfrom $t =-3$ to $t = 1$ (shown above)?" 13194139534701 false] [17592186092521 1145 "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534701 true] [17592186289504 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/assets/8868658c9bc7195f435a0109fce26b8a4fa39324c0a9a39e3fb644c5f02cdc9b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t),\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" 13194139534701 true] [17592186289504 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/8868658c9bc7195f435a0109fce26b8a4fa39324c0a9a39e3fb644c5f02cdc9b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t),\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" 13194139534701 false] [17592186304304 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304305 13194139534701 true] [17592186304304 1089 "q-10257" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304304 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534701 true] [17592186304304 1100 "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2{cos}^{3}⁡t,\\,y=2{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304304 1113 #uuid "fd387a77-72ef-5833-83c0-73cdf3cd884d" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304304 1145 "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{cos}^{3}⁡t)=-6{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{sin}^{3}⁡t)=6{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(-6{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(6{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{36{cos}^{4}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t+36{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{36{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(-1-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304306 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304307 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304308 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304309 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304310 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1041 "selection" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304307 13194139534701 true] [17592186304305 1110 #uuid "ce0eaa8c-5036-522e-97ea-b1d5ec6ad207" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304306 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304306 1111 #uuid "eaba7bba-53b5-5509-b334-f4da84149b7c" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304307 1034 "3" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304307 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304307 1111 #uuid "3ab95e35-7027-5a36-acd6-ca913286129c" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304308 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304308 1111 #uuid "e20f86aa-e684-58e6-92cf-1a4c7135d75c" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304309 1034 "1" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304309 1111 #uuid "f1d7eb29-18e9-5b97-949e-7bc4e9c60919" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304310 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304310 1111 #uuid "7bbbd4b1-18d0-55a9-a077-1f69d804375e" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304311 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304312 13194139534701 true] [17592186304311 1089 "q-10261" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304311 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534701 true] [17592186304311 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/assets/8288453c2625dac592a51054df332abf8ee49dbf8cbcabaf327c3ffe63b55f71.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304311 1113 #uuid "954304bc-c5f4-5131-95ba-54e09bfed3c0" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304311 1145 "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+4{cos}^{2}⁡t-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4+4-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the double-angle formula for cosine, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$ Substituting $\\theta =\\frac{t}{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{t}{2}) & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}) \\\\ 8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =16{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304313 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304314 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304315 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304316 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304317 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1041 "selection" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304315 13194139534701 true] [17592186304312 1110 #uuid "38bd5068-041d-5e13-96a4-7dbcc59c88b0" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304313 1034 "4\\pi " 13194139534701 true] [17592186304313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304313 1111 #uuid "445be6a6-0063-502b-9aac-23e37c7a323e" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304314 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304314 1111 #uuid "abb451af-ba20-5d14-9ac4-af61b67a6cd7" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304315 1034 "8" 13194139534701 true] [17592186304315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534701 true] [17592186304315 1111 #uuid "79ea321c-fe00-5a87-a86d-00591936b716" 13194139534701 true] [1